          "title": {
            "id": "you.title",
            "canonicalEnglish": "Run and manage CPN-based workflow factories"
          },
          "description": {
            "id": "you.description",
            "canonicalEnglish": "Run and manage CPN-based workflow factories.\n\nWhat:\nCPN-based workflow factory CLI for running factories, submitting work, and inspecting live sessions.\n\nHow to use:\nRun you run --work ./docs/examples/startup-work.json to start the current Factory with explicit Work and the local dashboard (http://localhost:7437/dashboard/ui).\nUse you run --dir factory --work ./docs/examples/startup-work.json for an explicit Factory directory. See you <cmd> --help for subcommand details.\n\nAgents:\nStart with you docs agents for orientation, you submit or you submit batch to enqueue work, and you session list to confirm a live factory.\nRun you docs for all packaged reference topics. Use --verbose or --debug for stderr diagnostics; full policy in you docs."
          }
        },
        "examples": [
          "you run --work ./docs/examples/startup-work.json",
          "you docs agents"
        ],
        "visibility": "public",
        "sourceHash": "e5e34cb36219695b80f23b06dbb0cb6d54cb481e806684543429c5aa5317175d"
      },
